    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1309">

                <pb facs="1132" n="818" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg818"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 855.48/28</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-17">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 17, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>275. Your 248, 5th. Department is informed by Ambassador Page, London, that the
                    British Government is cooperating with American Embassy in supplies for the
                    Belgians. Department <pb facs="1133" n="819" xml:id="pg819"/> would be pleased
                    to have some definite assurance from the French Government of its recognition of
                    the neutrality of goods shipped for International Commission for Relief in
                    Belgium.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
